1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,075
Cloud diagrams explain the components.

2
00:00:02,075 --> 00:00:06,311
But beginners also need to see why those components work together.

3
00:00:06,311 --> 00:00:09,006
Stack and Survive makes those decisions playable.

4
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:17,139
You operate a data center through one hundred eighty seconds of Black Friday.

5
00:00:17,139 --> 00:00:21,744
Traffic spikes, bots arrive, and every infrastructure choice affects customers and cost.

6
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:27,218
Start small, then build before the next wave.

7
00:00:27,218 --> 00:00:29,902
Adding an App machine takes eight seconds.

8
00:00:29,902 --> 00:00:34,120
Cache reduces eligible database reads, but order writes still reach SQL.

9
00:00:34,120 --> 00:00:37,571
Scale in or change tiers when your needs change.

10
00:00:37,571 --> 00:00:40,638
The current state, not the animation, determines capacity.

11
00:00:44,150 --> 00:00:49,876
During the bot attack, Protected Edge filters malicious requests, with a tradeoff in legitimate traffic.

12
00:00:49,876 --> 00:00:53,312
More App machines do not fix every database bottleneck.

13
00:00:53,312 --> 00:00:58,275
Watch the next wave, read the pressure, and choose which layer needs attention.

14
00:01:02,150 --> 00:01:05,490
The final wave reaches six hundred requests per second.

15
00:01:05,490 --> 00:01:09,573
This is edited footage of a real run, not accelerated simulation.

16
00:01:09,573 --> 00:01:13,284
Clear the full operation, then inspect what your decisions achieved.

17
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:19,020
This full run scored 9473 points.

18
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:21,411
Compare availability, cost and architecture.

19
00:01:21,411 --> 00:01:28,107
Try a different strategy, then follow Microsoft Learn links to explore the real services.

20
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:34,428
The implemented Export Agent connects finished runs to infrastructure as code.

21
00:01:34,428 --> 00:01:39,873
It can select mapping and validation tools, then repair a candidate using compiler feedback.

22
00:01:39,873 --> 00:01:44,151
These are real tool boundaries, not a chatbot controlling the game.

23
00:01:44,151 --> 00:01:46,873
Live Azure model verification is still pending.

24
00:01:46,873 --> 00:01:48,040
Nothing is deployed.

25
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:50,885
Play first.

26
00:01:50,885 --> 00:01:51,987
Question the tradeoff.

27
00:01:51,987 --> 00:01:53,457
Then explore Microsoft Learn.

28
00:01:53,457 --> 00:01:58,600
Try Stack and Survive, and see what you would change in the next architecture.
